	It's not like this is news or anything, but... nethack's
alignment system is severely messed up.

	I'm working on ascending a chaotic knight. Not one of these weak
"Oops, it's the wrong high altar, I'll just slap on a HoOA and ascend!"
deals, but keeping starting alignment only long enough to grab the Bell
and permanently converting ASAP after that.

	This involved not paying much attention to my nominal alignment
in the early game... my first ascension was a knight, and I was pretty
careful about avoiding "caitiff" situations, to the point of carrying a
bugle around to announce the commencement of hostilities when I found a
throne room or zoo or the like (just kicking a rock or something works,
too, but there's no style in that). This time... none of that. Killing
sleeping monsters? No problem! If they're running away, so much the
better! I killed peacefuls for their gear or intrinsics or just because
they were in my way. I killed a white unicorn for its horn. And I
finally made 14th level and went to talk to Arthur to get admitted to
the Quest... piously lawful! No problem, go right in!

	Well, so I went and killed Ixoth and grabbed the Bell and
Mirror, and on the way back, I killed the priestess on the Isle of Glass
and converted her altar with her own corpse. Then I went looking for a
white unicorn so I could finish the job proper-like (after determining
that I wasn't likely to get much but 'i's and 'j's out of the magic
traps on the Isle... I did take the time to kill some peaceful tengu for
TC and teleportitis, though), and on the way out, killed everyone in
Camelot, including all the pages and King Arthur. Then I went up to a
chaotic altar that I knew of and read a cursed scroll of create monster
in hopes of getting a white unicorn (I didn't), and after killing off
the other stuff that got dumped on me, I checked my status with my
stethoscope...

Status of Morgaine (piously lawful):  Level 14  HP 90(90)  AC -10, very
fast, invisible.--More--

	Piously lawful? I just killed my Quest Leader in cold blood! I
just slaughtered an entire castle full of pages! I just murdered a
peaceful priestess and used her corpse to perform a blood ritual to a
dark god on her own altar! Killing a couple dozen monsters is enough to
make up for that? This alignment system seriously needs some adjustment.

